    11	# on first use. A CLAUDE.local.md in that directory supplies the agent's
    12	# identity; without one the agent is generic and the name is just a label.
    13	# choirmaster is not registered anywhere — founding step 6 puts real content in
    14	# its directory, and this script treats it like any other name.
    15	#
    16	# Attach-or-create comes from tmux on the box: `tmux new-session -A` attaches
    17	# to the session named <name> when it exists and creates it when it does not,
    18	# so a closed iTerm2 window never orphans an agent — type the same command to
    19	# reconnect. Inside the session runs the handoff supervisor, which launches
    20	# the claude session, recycles it on every handoff, and exits when its agent
    21	# stops without handing off; the tmux session closes with it, so nothing
    22	# lingers. A second launch of a running name attaches instead of duplicating,
    23	# and the supervisor's own lock refuses a duplicate even if tmux is bypassed.
    24	# Both protections are per-machine, as is every other thing an agent owns, so
    25	# the same name used on both machines is simply two unrelated agents — no
    26	# conflict, only a label you cannot tell apart in a listing spanning both.
    27	#
    28	# --no-attach creates the session without attaching this terminal (for
